Jobs & Steps in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how jobs and steps control execution flow inside a GitHub Actions workflow.

🔹 Job Dependencies
Jobs can depend on other jobs using dependencies.
 This ensures:
Correct execution order
Controlled pipeline flow
Useful for multi-stage CI/CD.

🔹 Sequential vs Parallel Jobs
Jobs run in parallel by default
Dependencies make jobs run sequentially
Parallel jobs reduce pipeline time
Choosing wisely improves performance.

🔹 Step Execution Flow
Steps run sequentially inside a job.
 Each step:
Executes commands or actions
Shares the same runner environment

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Jobs define pipeline stages.
 Steps execute tasks.
 Dependencies control flow.
